  "interpretation": "The benchmark completed on the corrected pinned original GPT-2 FP32 CPU runtime. Capacity 1 and 2 never hit because the deterministic round-robin stream revisited each prefix only after three other distinct keys; both configurations thrashed and were slower than uncached execution. Capacity 4 retained all four keys: 176 hits, 16 cold misses across four repetitions, zero evictions, and 86,114,304 resident KV bytes. Its aggregate throughput improved 1.7651x, CPU time ratio was 0.5668, p95 latency ratio 0.9932 and sampled RSS ratio 1.0912. However, its minimum paired request speedup was 0.8615, below the frozen 0.90 minimum. Therefore no capacity passes all criteria: MULTIPREFIX_LRU_NO_GO. The four-entry design shows substantial cohort throughput potential, but fails the preregistered worst-request guardrail; this cannot be waived or averaged away.",
